dentity. It includes similar topic. Could also include six years timing? The requirement has multiple semantic conditions: article exists, similar topic, six years after book. Since no support, choose one facet. The most central is identify the journal article. But we shouldn't jump to title? The Original Question asks title. Parent requirement asks article. We can say "the journal article that is on a similar topic to the author's mathematics–ancient technique for liberation book and was published six years after that book." That's the residual.

Need output JSON exactly:
{
  "parent_requirement_id": "R5",
  "mode": "probe",
  "used_claims": [],
  "local_residual": "..."
}

Ensure no extra. The local_residual should not be a search query. It should be a statement of evidence objective. Something like "Establish the identity and existence of a journal article authored by the Indian author in question that is on a topic similar to their book connecting mathematics to an ancient technique for liberation, and establish its publication date relative to that book as six years later." That's maybe bundling multiple conditions. But okay? The instruction: If several independent unresolved parts remain, choose exactly ONE coherent part. The parent requirement has article existence/identity and timing. Could separate. Which part is most appropriate? Since no claims, probe. The exploratory evidence objective could be: "Whether the author published a journal article on a topic similar to their book connecting mathematics to an ancient technique for liberation." That's one part (article existence/topic). Then timing later. But the parent requirement includes timing. However local residual can be one coherent facet. The final answer title requires article identity. So choose: "Establish whether the author (the one who published the book connecting mathematics to an ancient technique for liberation) published a journal article on a similar topic." That's low-commitment and doesn't require timing yet. But if we leave timing out, we're not fully covering R5 but one facet. That's allowed. Maybe better to include "six years after the book" because it's part of the relation. But instruction says if several independent unresolved parts, choose exactly ONE coherent part. The timing is a separate condition from the article's topic. But the core target is the article. I'd set local_residual: "The journal article published by the Indian author on a topic similar to their book connecting mathematics to an ancient technique for liberation, including its identity/title, remains to be established." That's one objective. It doesn't mention six years, but the parent requirement's timing is another facet. However the question asks title, so this is the direct target. Mode probe.

